.TH MGIT 1 "2026-10-13" "Knowledge Islands" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
\&
.PP
mgit \- run commands across multiple Git repositories
.SH SYNOPSIS
\&
.SS General
\&
.TP
.B mgit
List the primary checkouts in the current set.
.sp
.TP
.B mgit [\fIoptions\fR] [\fIcommand\fR ...]
Run
.B git
with the supplied command and arguments in every selected checkout, several
at once, and report the checkouts with output or a failure.
.TP
.B mgit [\fIoptions\fR] \-R \fIcommand\fR [\fIargument\fR ...]
Run a command directly, without prefixing it with
.BR git ,
in every repository in the current set.
.TP
.B mgit [\fIoptions\fR] \-G \fIgit-command\fR [\fIargument\fR ...]
Run a Git subcommand in every selected checkout even when
.B mgit
owns the name, as in
.BR "mgit \-G worktree list" .
.SS Workspace management
\&
.TP
.B mgit register
Generate
.I .mgit.toml
manifests for the current tree.
.sp
.TP
.B mgit repair [\-\-apply]
Preview a recognised legacy schema repair and missing repository clones.
Apply both only with
.BR \-\-apply .
Existing repository paths are never replaced.
The selection comes from the current
.I .mgit.toml
manifest.
.TP
.B mgit doctor
Evaluate Git availability and the current manifest without mutation.
Show execution context, check scope, verdict and pass/warn/fail/skipped counts.
An absent optional manifest is healthy; package updates and repository
synchronization are not checked.
.TP
.B mgit diag [\-\-full]
Print tool/version, installation mode, host platform/architecture, executing
Bash runtime and configuration state. Local paths and configuration error
details require full output. Installation is local for a linked or directly
invoked checkout, release for an installed package with receipt evidence, or
unknown when provenance cannot be established.
.SS Repository management
\&
.TP
.B mgit sync [-i|--interactive] [-v|--verbose]
Fetch in parallel, then fast-forward or push clean tracking branches in the
current set, and summarize repositories that changed or need attention.
.TP
.B mgit overview [--json] [-v|--verbose] [--stale-days <days>]
Show, read-only, what is outstanding across the current set.
.TP
.B mgit structure <standard|nested> [--dry-run]
Convert every eligible repository in the current set between standard and
nested structures.
.TP
.B mgit worktree \fIlist|status\fR
List worktrees or show their branch and cleanliness.
.TP
.B mgit worktree add \fIBRANCH\fR
Add a linked checkout for an existing remote branch in every structured
repository.
.TP
.B mgit worktree remove <path> [--force]
Remove one linked worktree.
.SS Shell integration
\&
.TP
.B mgit completion <shell>
Print shell completion source.
.TP
.B mgit help [\fICOMMAND\fR [\fISUBCOMMAND\fR]]
Print contextual help for an mgit command.
.SH DESCRIPTION
\&
.B mgit
runs a Git command, or an arbitrary command with
.BR \-R ,
across a set of repositories.
It runs up to
.B \-\-jobs
checkouts at once, capturing each one's output, and draws one progress line on
standard error when that is a terminal.
When every checkout has finished it prints, in selection order, the checkout
label and command followed by the captured output for each checkout that
printed anything or failed, then one summary line counting quiet checkouts,
checkouts with output and failures, and naming each failed checkout with its
exit status.
A checkout that exits 0 without output is quiet.
Any
.B git status
(or a Git alias for one, such as
.BR "st = status -sb" )
is quiet exactly when the checkout has no changes and is level with an
upstream.
With no command it prints the checkout labels that would be used.
.PP
Commands run with standard input from
.IR /dev/null ,
.B GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0
and
.B GIT_EDITOR
and
.B GIT_SEQUENCE_EDITOR
set to
.BR false ,
so a command that would prompt or open an editor fails instead of waiting
unseen; run it with
.B \-\-verbose
instead.
Captured output carries no colour.
.PP
The reserved command tree consists of
.BR register ,
.BR repair ,
.BR sync ,
.BR overview ,
.BR structure ,
.BR worktree ,
.BR completion ,
and
.BR help .
Their subcommands and arguments are validated by
.BR mgit .
Other commands are passed to Git unchanged, so
.B mgit status --short
means the same Git command in every selected repository.
.PP
Command headers and sync progress use checkout labels. A linked worktree
outside its repository appears as repository [branch], while execution uses
the real checkout path. ANSI styling appears only on a terminal; a non-empty
.B NO_COLOR
disables it there as well.
.B mgit help \fICOMMAND\fR
and
.B mgit \fICOMMAND\fR --help
print help scoped to that command.
.PP
When the current directory contains a
.I .mgit.toml
manifest,
.B mgit
uses the workspace's direct members, recursively expanding each child workspace.
Existing schema-1 manifests still select their configured default group.
The manifest is only valid in a non-Git container directory.
.PP
A repository leaf may contain
.IR .mgit.toml .
That file declares only cross-repository symlink metadata; it does not select
repositories or make a workspace.
.PP
Without a workspace manifest,
.B mgit
walks the current tree for Git repositories, omitting repositories nested
inside another repository.
Discovery stops at repository roots and never follows symlinked repositories
or container directories by default.
The
.B \-I
option ignores workspace manifests and always uses discovery instead.
.PP
With
.BR \-t / \-\-territory ,
.BR \-\-estate
or
.BR \-\-principals ,
.B mgit
invokes
.B ki territory roots --null --territory HANDLE
once and uses the returned local repository roots as its exact set.
This optional mode does not read KI configuration itself and requires
.B ki
on
.BR PATH .
.SH INSTALLATION
\&
.PP
The human-facing tool page is
.I https://knowledgeislands.info/projects/mgit/ .
.PP
On macOS or Linux, install the published release with Homebrew:
.PP
.nf
brew install knowledgeislands/tap/mgit
.fi
.PP
On any system with Bash and Git, install the current release with:
.PP
.nf
curl -fsSL https://knowledgeislands.info/install/mgit | bash
.fi
.PP
Pass an exact release with:
.PP
.nf
curl -fsSL https://knowledgeislands.info/install/mgit | bash -s -- vX.Y.Z
.fi
.PP
The installer writes the executable to
.I ~/.local/bin
and the manual to
.I ~/.local/share/man/man1
by default. Set
.B MGIT_INSTALL_DIR
or
.B MGIT_MAN_INSTALL_DIR
to choose different locations. Set
.B MGIT_VERSION
as an exact-version environment alias. A positional version takes precedence;
with neither input, the installer discovers the latest release.
.SH OPTIONS
\&
.TP
.BR \-P , " \-\-physical"
When discovering repositories, do not enter symlinked directories.
This is the default.
Discovery happens only when the current directory has no workspace manifest,
or with
.BR \-\-ignore ;
the option has no effect on a manifest's declared members.
.sp
.TP
.BR \-L , " \-\-follow-symlinks"
When discovering repositories, also enter symlinked directories that contain
repositories.
A symlink to a repository itself is never followed.
.sp
.TP
.BR \-G , " \-\-git"
Pass every argument to
.BR git ,
even a command name that
.B mgit
owns, such as
.BR worktree ,
.BR sync
or
.BR help .
It takes the same selectors as an ordinary command and cannot be combined with
.BR \-R .
The name is temporary:
.B \-B
returns later as the bypass-to-Git flag in its place.
.sp
.TP
.BR \-R , " \-\-raw"
Run the supplied command directly rather than as a
.B git
subcommand.
The arguments are executed as given, not through a shell; use
.B sh \-c
for pipes and redirections.
.sp
.TP
.BR \-j , " \-\-jobs " \fIn\fR
Run up to
.I n
checkouts at once for ordinary commands and
.BR overview ,
or fetches at once for
.BR sync .
The default is 8;
.B \-j 1
runs one at a time.
.sp
.TP
.BR \-v , " \-\-verbose"
Run an ordinary command in one checkout at a time, streaming every header and
all output as it happens, with the terminal attached and no summary line.
With
.B overview
or
.BR sync ,
the same as its own
.BR \-\-verbose .
.sp
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print an ordinary command's results as one JSON document: the command, each
checkout's label, path, exit status, quiet flag, standard output and standard
error, and the counts.
With
.BR overview ,
the same as its own
.BR \-\-json .
It cannot be combined with
.BR \-\-verbose .
.sp
.TP
.BR \-I , " \-\-ignore"
Ignore
.I .mgit.toml
workspace selection and discover repositories by walking the tree.
Repository-kind symlink metadata still expands the discovered set.
.sp
.TP
.BR \-t , " \-\-territory" " \fINAME\fR"
Select the local roots resolved by
.B ki
for the territory handle.
MGit uses the resolver's NUL-delimited output. Ordinary commands invoke
.B ki
only when this selector is present. This selector cannot be combined with
.BR \-P ,
.BR \-L ,
.BR \-I ,
and it is unavailable to MGit management commands except
.BR register .
.sp
.TP
.B \-\-estate
Select every local root in the registered KI estate. It calls
.B ki territory roots --null --estate
and cannot be combined with
.BR \-\-territory .
It has the same restrictions but is unavailable to
.BR register .
.sp
.TP
.B \-\-principals
Select the territory Capitals. It calls
.B ki territory roots --null --principals
and keeps its order: Knowledge Islands Principal first, then the other
Capitals alphabetically by territory name.
It cannot be combined with
.B \-\-territory
or
.B \-\-estate
and has the same restrictions as
.BR \-\-estate .
.sp
.TP
.BR \-f , " \-\-filter" " \fIPREFIX\fR"
Select logical repository directory basenames beginning with the nonempty
literal, case-sensitive
.IR PREFIX .
The option is repeatable with OR semantics; glob characters are literal.
Filters apply before linked-worktree expansion and never match checkout names.
Explicit KI scopes pass filters to the producer before physical-root checks;
excluded unavailable registered roots do not block selection.
Default discovery and saved snapshots apply the same predicate locally without
KI.
Empty prefixes and zero matches fail before dispatch.
.sp
.TP
.BR \-W , " \-\-all-worktrees"
Include every active linked worktree as well as the primary checkout when
listing repositories or running ordinary commands,
.B sync
and
.BR overview .
Normal listings and command headers label worktrees outside the repository or
under its hidden Git storage as repository [branch], without the storage prefix.
Detached worktrees use their directory name and abbreviated commit.
Execution still uses the actual checkout path; use
.B worktree list
to inspect physical paths.
Without this option, a standard repository uses its root checkout and a nested
repository uses its required
.I main/
checkout.
.B structure
and
.B worktree
management commands reject this option.
.sp
.TP
.BR \-h , " \-\-help"
Print contextual help for the requested command and exit.
.sp
.TP
.BR \-V , " \-\-version"
Print the version and exit.
Global discovery selectors apply to listing, ordinary commands,
.BR sync ,
.BR overview ,
.BR structure ,
and
.BR worktree .
Only ordinary command pass-through accepts
.B \-G
and
.BR \-R .
.B register
accepts
.B \-a
as a saved-location shorthand;
.B repair
accept no global selector. Inapplicable selectors produce a usage error
before a management command runs. Help and version remain available.
.SH COMMAND GROUPS
\&
.PP
mGit divides its commands into workspace management, repository management,
and shell integration. Run
.B mgit help
for the command list and
.B mgit help \fICOMMAND\fR
for exact command grammar.
.SS Workspace management
\&
.TP
.B mgit register
scans saved locations (default:
.BR local )
and writes a
.I .mgit.toml
in every non-Git container directory, listing child workspaces and repositories.
It writes a
.I .mgit.toml
only in a repository that owns cross-repository symlinks.
The command does not descend into repositories and refreshes direct members.
.B mgit register add
and
.B mgit register rm
change saved search locations and refresh generated entries in one invocation.
Both accept repeated and combined
.B \-\-territory
.I NAME
and
.B \-\-repo
.I PATH
options.
.B mgit register \-\-territory
.I NAME
is an add shorthand. Adding a repository path requires an existing Git
repository; removal accepts a saved relative path even after it disappears.
Later runs of
.B mgit register
refresh all saved locations, resolving territory roots through
.BR ki .
Source resolution failure stops registration before writing. Ordinary commands
use generated repository entries without invoking
.BR ki .
Each location root outside the workspace is written as an ordinary external
repository member; a root that local discovery already records is not written
again. A repository reached from several workspaces is dispatched once.
.B mgit repair
validates present external members but never clones a missing one.
.B mgit register \-\-dry\-run
previews manifest writes and removals, including location changes,
without changing local files or Chezmoi source state. Registration still
validates locations before the preview.
.PP
When Chezmoi is installed and configured, generated manifests below its target
directory are added to Chezmoi's source state when possible. A Chezmoi failure
emits a warning but does not prevent a local manifest from being generated or
removed.
.TP
.B mgit repair
uses the workspace manifest in the current directory to preview every missing
repository among the direct members with a source URL.
On apply it creates standard, nested, and bare repositories in their declared
forms.
It recursively follows child workspaces through their direct members.
External members, whose paths begin with
.BR ../ ,
are reported when missing and never cloned.
.B mgit repair \-\-apply
performs the validated config repair and missing repository clones.
Repair validates the workspace before the preview; without
.B \-\-apply
it does not change files.
Existing paths are never replaced: a present repository must match its declared
structure, and child workspace directories and manifests must already exist.
.SS Repository management
\&
.TP
.B mgit sync
first fetches, in parallel, the upstream remote of every selected clean branch
that tracks one, once per repository and remote.
Then, one checkout at a time in selection order, it compares each branch with
its upstream.
A branch only behind is fast-forwarded with
.BR "git merge \-\-ff\-only" ;
a branch only ahead runs
.BR "git push" .
Nothing is merged or rebased, whatever
.B pull.rebase
says.
Worktrees with local changes print
.B git status \-\-short
and are skipped, as are detached heads, branches without an upstream, diverged
branches and checkouts whose fetch failed; each is named with a warning and
left untouched.
With
.BR \-i " or " \-\-interactive ,
it asks before each pull and push; an empty answer skips the action.
Declined actions are counted at the end and do not cause failure.
If input ends before an answer, the command stops unsuccessfully.
.PP
Only repositories that pulled, pushed, warned or failed are named.
Already-current repositories are collapsed into one final count and bare
repositories into another.
With
.BR \-v " or " \-\-verbose ,
it also prints numbered progress for each checkout, names each bare
repository, and announces each pull and push before it starts.
Any warning, failure or bare repository makes the command exit unsuccessfully.
.TP
.B mgit overview
reads local Git state only, never fetching or changing a ref, the index or a
stash, and reports for each selected checkout its branch and upstream, ahead
and behind counts, staged, modified, untracked and conflicted files, stashes,
prunable or detached linked worktrees, and obsolete branches.
A local branch is obsolete when it is merged into the default branch
.RI ( origin/HEAD ,
else
.I main
or
.IR master ),
patch-equivalent to it, has a gone upstream, or is unmerged and idle beyond
.B \-\-stale-days
(default 30); a remote-tracking branch is obsolete when merged or stale.
Automation branches are judged alike and marked. A branch checked out in any
worktree is never obsolete. Stashes, worktrees and branches are reported once
per repository when
.B \-W
lists several of its checkouts.
.PP
Only checkouts that need attention are named, each on one line with its
findings and an indented line per obsolete branch; a closing line counts clean,
attention and failed checkouts.
.B \-v
or
.B \-\-verbose
names clean checkouts too, and
.B \-\-json
prints one JSON document with every checkout and the counts.
The command exits 1 only when a checkout cannot be read.
.TP
.B mgit structure nested
converts each eligible clean, attached standard checkout to a nested repository.
.B mgit structure standard
performs the reverse conversion only when the nested repository has its required
.I main/
checkout and no other linked worktrees.
.PP
Both forms apply changes by default.
Pass
.B \-\-dry-run
to preview changes instead.
.TP
.B mgit worktree list
groups linked worktrees by their shared Git store.
.B mgit worktree status
shows each worktree's branch and cleanliness.
.PP
.B mgit worktree add \fIBRANCH\fR
adds a checkout for an existing
.B origin/\fIBRANCH\fR
to every structured repository after preflighting the full set. Nested
repositories receive
.I <repository>/<branch>
checkouts; standard repositories receive
.I <repository>/.git/mgit-worktrees/<branch>
checkouts.
.B mgit worktree remove <path>
removes one linked checkout and never removes the primary or required
.I main/
checkout.
Pass
.B \-\-force
to discard dirty changes in that linked checkout.
.SS Shell integration
\&
.TP
.B mgit completion bash
and
.B mgit completion zsh
print shell completion definitions to standard output.
They complete the command hierarchy and command-local flags.
.PP
For Bash, source the definition from the shell configuration:
.PP
.nf
source <(mgit completion bash)
.fi
.PP
For Zsh, write the definition to a file named
.I _mgit
in a directory on
.B fpath
before
.B compinit
runs. For example:
.PP
.nf
mkdir -p ~/.zsh/completions
mgit completion zsh > ~/.zsh/completions/_mgit
fpath=(~/.zsh/completions $fpath)
autoload -Uz compinit && compinit
.fi
.SH FILES
\&
.SS Workspace kind
\&
.PP
A
.I .mgit.toml
manifest uses an explicit workspace kind and path-keyed direct members.
The complete generated shape is:
.PP
.nf
kind = "workspace"
locations = ["local"]

[members."platform"]
kind = "repository"
type = "standard"
source = "git@github.com:acme/platform.git"

[members."workspace"]
kind = "repository"
type = "nested"

[members."archive.git"]
kind = "repository"
type = "bare"

[members."group"]
kind = "workspace"
.fi
.PP
Repository members require
.BR type ,
which is one of
.BR standard ,
.BR nested ,
or
.BR bare .
The optional
.B source
field is a clone URL. Workspace members use only
.BR kind .
Member paths are safe relative map keys below the manifest directory. A
repository member may instead be external: one or more leading
.B ../
segments followed by a safe relative path, such as
.BR ../../.local/share/chezmoi .
External members are generated from saved locations and rewritten by
registration, which names each hand-written external member it drops.
An external path that resolves back inside the manifest directory is
rejected. A missing external member fails selection, as a missing local
member does.
.PP
The
.B locations
array stores search source strings such as
.BR local ,
.BR territory:short ,
and
.BR repo:../shared-tools .
When absent, it defaults to
.BR local .
Empty
.B [registered.members."PATH"]
tables from earlier releases remain readable for selection with a deprecation
warning;
.B mgit register
rewrites them as typed members, and
.B mgit doctor
reports them as a warning. Old Agora locations,
fields and member tables, including schema-1 Agora
snapshots, are rejected without automatic migration or aliases.
.PP
Existing schema-1 manifests with grouped members remain readable.
Registration migrates one containing only the structural default group to
direct members. A manifest with alternative groups must have those tables
removed deliberately before registration; mgit refuses to discard them.
.B mgit repair
previews the exact diff without writing or refreshing membership.
.B mgit repair \-\-apply
revalidates and writes only a recognised repository manifest or a workspace
with a sole structural default group. Unknown shapes and alternative groups
are refused. This does not update Chezmoi source state.
.SS Repository kind
\&
.PP
Repository-owned
.I .mgit.toml
files have a separate leaf-only purpose: their
.B symlinks
table maps a symlink the current repository owns to its target in another
repository:
.PP
.nf
kind = "repository"

[symlinks]
"link" = "target"
.fi
.PP
Blank lines and comments beginning with
.B #
are ignored.
.SH REPOSITORY STRUCTURES
\&
.PP
A standard repository is an ordinary checkout with a
.I .git/
directory. Worktrees added by
.B mgit
are placed below
.IR .git/mgit-worktrees/ .
A nested repository is an
.B mgit
controller containing a
.I .bare/
shared Git store, a
.I .git
controller file, and a required
.I main/
checkout.
Commands operate in live checkouts, never in the nested controller or bare
store.
.SH DEVELOPMENT INSTALLATIONS
\&
.PP
For development against this checkout, run
.B ./install.sh --link
to link the current executable and manual into
.B MGIT_INSTALL_DIR
(default
.IR ~/.local/bin )
and
.B MGIT_MAN_INSTALL_DIR
(default: the corresponding
.IR share/man/man1
directory). The linked command follows changes to this checkout and does not
download a release.
.PP
Link mode refuses to replace regular files. Use a dedicated development
directory or invoke
.B ./bin/mgit
directly when comparing it with a Homebrew or release installation. Use
.B man -l man/mgit.1
to inspect the checked-out manual regardless of the configured manual path.
.SH EXIT STATUS
\&
.TP
.B 0
The requested operation completed successfully.
.sp
.TP
.B 1
An operation failed.
.sp
.TP
.B 2
The command grammar was invalid or an unsupported option was supplied.
.PP
For a fan-out command,
.B mgit
returns status 1 if any selected repository command fails, after attempting
every selected checkout. It returns 0 only when every command succeeds.
An interrupt stops the run, removes its temporary files and exits 130, or 143
for a termination signal.
.SH SEE ALSO
\&
.BR git (1),
.BR git-worktree (1)
.PP
The project README and the guide collection are available at
.I https://github.com/knowledgeislands/tools-mgit .
.PP
The user guide lives under
.I docs/guides/user/
in that repository:
.I installation.md
covers installation and upgrades,
.I running-commands.md
covers command fan-out and selectors,
.I repository-sets.md
covers
.I .mgit.toml
manifests and registration, and
.I worktrees.md
covers the standard and nested repository structures.

.SH TERRITORY MIGRATION
\&
.PP
Old
.B \-a/\-\-agora
selectors and
.B agora:
locations are retired.
Back up the manifest and any managed source, explicitly replace saved locations
with verified
.B territory:HANDLE
values in a reviewed copy, and remove the old agora field and member tables.
Preserve local members and user settings.
Run
.B mgit register \-\-dry\-run
and inspect the proposed membership before explicitly refreshing with
.BR "mgit register" .
Resolution or output validation failure leaves the manifest unchanged.
Ordinary generated snapshots remain offline and never silently refresh.
Use a literal prefix such as
.B tools\-
in place of a historic glob such as tools\-*.
The roots endpoint is buffered completely; partial output, malformed NUL
framing,
duplicates, missing roots or registrations and ambiguous handles stop dispatch.
